      <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow">ByteDance engineering interview preparation</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>LeetCode volume matters.</strong> ByteDance algorithm rounds are harder than most FAANG interviews. 200+ problems solved at medium-hard difficulty is a realistic preparation floor. Focus on DP, graphs, trees, and string algorithms — these appear most frequently in ByteDance screening.</li>
        <li><strong>Explain complexity at every step.</strong> ByteDance interviewers want clean code plus clear time and space complexity analysis. Practice narrating your approach, identifying bottlenecks, and optimizing iteratively — not just producing a working solution.</li>
        <li><strong>System design at TikTok scale.</strong> Prepare for: video recommendation feed, content delivery network for short-form video, creator analytics pipeline, real-time comment and interaction systems, and ad serving at high throughput. Each of these reflects actual ByteDance infrastructure challenges.</li>
        <li><strong>Behavioral: speed and impact.</strong> ByteDance culture values what you shipped and how fast. Stories about building fast, iterating on feedback, and driving high output — even at the cost of polish — resonate better than stories about careful, long-cycle projects.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="content-panel">
